A||||8||G25C||Check engine light
Z||000000||G25C||07-18-99||02:18 AM||||<br>I have a 87 GT that when i start up in the morning or at night after work.  It imediately stalls.  If i give it a some gas for a few seconds it stays running and then i can drive it like normal. (it only does this on cold starts)<p>My brother said that maybe i need to change the fuel filter.  <p>The question about the Check engine light is this,<p>I have put 2000 miles on this GT since ive owned it (it had 94K when i bought it).  Atleast 5 times now the check engine light has come on only when i have shifted from 3rd to 4th at over 3500 rpms.  Nothing noticable happens when it does this, it drives and runs just fine.  When i shut the car off the light goes off and never comes back on...unless i go past 3500 rpms when shifting from 3rd to 4th.<p>I havnt check the engine light codes yet, i was wondering if anyone had a idea?
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||07-18-99||06:55 AM||||Pull the codes from the ECM first, that would eliminate a lot of guesswork. But I suspect you'll get a code 32...<p>The stalling after starting the car is AFAIK not something to worry about (if it is, I'm sure someone will correct me here). My 86.5GT does that too from time to time and it usually goes away after resetting the ECM.
Z||000002||mwbackus||07-18-99||09:56 AM||||Sounds like a malfunctioning cold start valve to me..
Z||000003||G25C||07-18-99||07:39 PM||||Your right Cliff, i did get the 32.  I looked up the code on the Online Decoding Service (on the internet) and it listed all codes (Haynes does also). The online form also gives information on what to do after getting the code and feedback from other drivers on how they fixed it.<p>I checked the plastic line and didnt find any cracks on it, but a rubber hose that had been attached to it and then to the EGR was severly loose.  I put a tighter hose on it.<p>Something else, On top of the EGR was a piece of duct tape covering it.  It was weathered pretty bad so i peeled it back to see what was under it and theres a hole in the top of the EGR and i can see some kind of air (bleeder?) type hole set into the EGR.  Is there soposed to be a hole on top of this?  Could this be letting out vacuum?<p>(insidently, i place a pump on the EGR and pumped it up, the Fiero tryed to stall.  Just like the book said it should if its a good Valve).<p>
Z||000004||G25C||07-18-99||08:29 PM||||I had reset the ECM code and took my GT for a test drive.  While shifting from 3rd to 4th at higher rpms...the light popped back on again.  (maybe it needs that piece of duct tape?)<p>
Z||000005||Cliff Pennock||07-19-99||06:19 AM||||No, there shouldn't be a hole there...
Z||000006||DJRice||07-19-99||02:33 PM||||Speaking of that Cold Start Valve... Is that a hard gadget to replace, My v6 does the same thing, But I just was content with giving it some warm up time.<p>
Z||000007||theogre||07-19-99||03:05 PM||||cold start,,,, I thought they did away with that in 86.5-87.... they reprogrammed the ECM to run the mains richer when cold.... <p>If there is any doubt of the EGR condition, replace it. There is not any reliable way to test it. Make sure the EGR controller solinoid is OK.
Z||000008||mwbackus||07-19-99||07:11 PM||||Cold start valves exist on all fiero v6's.  They are a bit of a challenge to replace, since you have to pretty good access the fuel rail.  I suspect that it could very well just be the circuit (ie.wiring, connectors)to the CS valve.  I would check this very carefully.  I suspect that the code 32 is a different problem entirely, EGR related of course, and you should still look towards the Cold Start valve problem for your starting problems.<p>Mike
